Description: CVE-2026-79921 - enforce AMQP minimum frame size during negotiation
 The client accepted whatever frame-max the server advertised during
 connection.tune negotiation, even values below the AMQP 0.9.1 minimum of
 4096 bytes. A malicious or misconfigured server could force an extremely
 small frame size, causing excessive fragmentation and CPU overhead
 (denial of service). This backports upstream PR #353 (commit 6beb7b51)
 which introduces negotiateFrameSize() to clamp the negotiated frame size
 to a floor of frameMinSize (4096).
Origin: backport, https://github.com/rabbitmq/amqp091-go/commit/6beb7b51f59e46ddcf8066ad498dad32491d3be0
